[h1]Droppable Weapons[/h1]

Allows you to physically drop your weapons and pick them back up again.

[i]This addon requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3329679071]AlyxLib[/url] to work.[/i]
[i]This addon is compatible with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3692545530]Akimbo Pistols[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3144612716]Body Holsters[/url][/i]

[h2]How To Use[/h2]

Grip your controller while the weapon is equipped, then release the grip to drop the weapon. Grab the weapon again with the same hand to re-equip it.

If you've dropped an Akimbo weapon you [i]must[/i] pick it up with your off-hand to equip it.

[h2]Console Commands[/h2]

Console commands allow you to customize and tweak the addon while playing. They are not required to use the addon, and for most users the default values will provide a good experience.

If you don't know how to use the console, follow this guide: https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2040205272

[hr][/hr]
[list]

[*][b]droppable_weapons_always_use_weapon_model[/b]
Default = 0
If enabled, the dropped physics proxy will always use the weapon model instead of a custom one if set.
[i]This convar is persistent with your save file.[/i]

[/list]

[hr][/hr]
Console commands can be set in the [url=https://help.steampowered.com/faqs/view/7D01-D2DD-D75E-2955]launch options[/url] for Half-Life: Alyx, just put a hyphen before each name and the value after, e.g. [b]-droppable_weapons_always_use_weapon_model 1[/b]
They can also be added to your [b]Half-Life Alyx\game\hlvr\cfg\skill.cfg[/b] file, one per line without the hyphen, e.g. [b]droppable_weapons_always_use_weapon_model 1[/b]

